<title>INDIA: India Crompton Greaves 96/97 net slumps.</title>
<headline>India Crompton Greaves 96/97 net slumps.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	     307.6     vs	   640.4</p>
<p>    Sales		 15,088.1     vs	14,807.3</p>
<p>    Other income	    88.8     vs	   15.49</p>
<p>    Expenditure	 13,771.6     vs	13,372.9</p>
<p>    Interest		 776.3     vs	   575.7</p>
<p>    Gross profit	   628.9     vs	 1,013.6</p>
<p>    Depreciation	   321.3     vs	   213.2</p>
<p>    Tax			  0.0     vs	   160.0</p>
<p>(after write back of earlier tax provision of 35 million)  </p>
<p>Note: Electrical equipment maker Crompton Greaves, part of the private Thapar Group, said its paid up share capital rose to 520.4 million rupees during the year, up from 453 million in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
